This is an altered source distribution for generated9, built with the native
Plan 9 compiler and libraries. The platform backends, build files, examples
and tests are generated9 contributions under the root LICENSE.

Port changes:
- Native rio, /dev/kbd, /dev/snarf, plumber, directory and timer interfaces.
- Classic OpenGL rendering through generated9's TinyGL/VirGL implementation.
- Native /dev/audio output; the upstream mixer, codecs and miniaudio data
  converters are retained. Native QLocks implement their synchronization.
- C library includes and scalar math operations adapted for native libc.
- Explicit packed Color and Vector3 component arrays, incomplete audio types,
  packed IQM wire structures, named arrays and local matrix temporaries for
  the native compiler.
- Vorbis temporary allocations use the heap with matching frees. An explicit
  int promotion preserves its negative floor-class sentinel under Plan 9
  integer promotion rules (2c(1)).
- Portable bit scanning and native file information; generic file errors in
  codecs instead of a fabricated POSIX errno. Unused wide-file entry points
  in miniaudio/MP3 are unavailable; raylib's UTF-8 file names remain supported.
- Explicit undefinitions in stb_image_resize2 where repeated inclusion would
  otherwise redefine macros rejected by Plan 9 cpp.

- FileRename converts successful native wstat byte counts to raylib's zero
  success result and supports rename within one directory.
- Model/material validity checks honor the classic renderer, which does not
  use shader IDs or vertex buffer objects.

Public raylib.h, raymath.h and rlgl.h are installed in /sys/include.
raymath9.h supplies native float-math adapters shared with the port.

Only dependencies of the configured native build are included. Foreign
window backends, software GL, FLAC and build systems are omitted.
